<h2>Your Quick-Start Checklist</h2>

<ol>
  <li><strong>Set a daily alarm.</strong> Same time every day. I used 6:30 AM before work. Some people prefer lunch breaks or right after dinner. Pick one and protect it.</li>
  <li><strong>Start with a baseline week.</strong> Do 15 questions per day across all domains. Don&rsquo;t study beforehand. Just see where you are. Record your scores.</li>
  <li><strong>Begin the domain rotation.</strong> One domain per day, Monday through Friday. Saturday is your weakest domain. Sunday is off.</li>
  <li><strong>Track everything.</strong> Date, domain, score, weakest concept. A simple spreadsheet is all you need.</li>
  <li><strong>Trust the process for 10 weeks.</strong> You will have bad days. You will have weeks where your scores plateau. Keep going. The compound effect of 70+ focused sessions is enormous.</li>
</ol>

<p>You don&rsquo;t need a $700 bootcamp. You don&rsquo;t need to read the entire CFR. You need 30 minutes a day, the right questions, and the discipline to show up.</p>

<p>You&rsquo;ve got this.</p>

